            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Furnace combustion air supply

- Some windows

- Wood fireplace

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. 

</airSeal>
                <AdditionalComments>ELECTRICAL CONSUMPTION



 Concerning your electrical usage, I?????????ve listed some solutions/problems that might be useful to help you find what seems to be causing the problem. The Following items might explain and help you to investigate:



1-      APPLIANCES/DEVICES: It is possible in some case that one of the appliances or devices use more energy than expected.



SOLUTION: Turn off your electrical panel and turn on one by one the breakers one by one and take a look at your electric meter to see if you notice a higher usage. This option might help you to aim at which one seems to drain Energy.

Proceed with the same strategy with the other brokers to verify if the consumption comes from another circuit.



2-      ELECTRICAL WIRES: In some cases, the wires come in contact with the electrical box (switch or plugs). In this case, the current will flow continuously, which can explain the higher usage. This situation can be caused by a natural movement of the house that has for effect to pull on the wires at the point of exposing the wires at the point of touching the metal box.



3-      ELECTRICAL USAGE MONITOR: Another option is to use an electricity usage monitor to verify the electrical usage of your appliances/devices and verify if they are similar, close, or higher than the specified by the manufacturer.



If the electrical meter runs faster than normal when you turn on the breaker of the appliances/devices or circuit, it might be an indicator. This procedure might help you to find what is causing the increase in your consumption and select the one that seems to be wrong.



I suggest starting with these suggestions and see if you can find something, hopefully, it will help you find the problem. The report gives you an estimated electrical usage, which you can compare with your electrical usage on your electric bills.



I wish you good luck and sincerely hope that you will find the problem. I will be curious to be informed if you find something or if the suggested solutions were helpful.

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
